The `stacks-node mainnet` and `stacks-node testnet` subcommands are deprecated in favor of `stacks-node start --mainnet` and `stacks-node start --testnet`. The old forms still work but now log a deprecation warning at startup. `start` accepts at most one of `--config <PATH>`, `--mainnet` or `--testnet`; supplying none of them joins mainnet, so `stacks-node start` on its own is equivalent to `stacks-node start --mainnet`.
